l the fish is cooked and flakes easily. Optionally, add cheese and let it melt for an additional 3 minutes after turning off the oven.\", \"Step 1: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).  \\nStep 2: Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.  \\nStep 3: Place the fillets on a baking sheet, optionally spray the sheet with butter-flavored cooking spray.  \\nStep 4: Bake in the preheated oven until the fish is cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.  \\nStep 5: Optionally, after the fish is fully cooked, turn off the oven, place slices of cheese on each fillet, and return to the oven for about 3 minutes until the cheese melts.  \\n\\nAnswer: To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the fillets with paprika and black pepper, place them on a baking sheet, and bake for about 15 minutes until the fish is cooked and flakes easily. Optionally, add cheese and let it melt for about 3 minutes after turning off the oven.\", \"Step 1: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\nStep 2: Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\nStep 3: Place the fillets on a baking sheet, optionally sprayed with butter-flavored cooking spray.\\nStep 4: Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish is cooked and flakes easily.\\nStep 5: (Optional) Turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return to the oven for about 3 minutes to melt the cheese.\\n\\nAnswer: To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place them on a baking sheet, optionally sprayed with butter-flavored cooking spray, and bake for about 15 minutes until the fish is cooked and flakes easily. Optionally, add cheese and return to the oven for about 3 minutes to melt.\"]", "time_sec": 159.149, "generation_time_seconds": 159.1463, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc