ts with paprika and black pepper, and bake for approximately 15 minutes until the fish is cooked and easily flakes. Optionally, after baking, add cheese and return to the oven for 3 minutes to melt.\", \"Step 1: Read and analyze the provided passages to understand how pollock is cooked.\\n\\nFrom passage 1:\\n- Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray.\\n- Season pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n- Place fillets on the baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n- Bake in a preheated oven until the fish is cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n\\nFrom passage 2:\\n- Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n- Season pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n- Bake in the preheated oven until the fish is cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n\\nFrom passage 3:\\n- Bake in a preheated oven until the fish is cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n- Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n- Return the fish to the oven to melt the cheese for about 3 minutes.\\n\\nStep 2: Synthesize the steps across all three passages to get a complete method for cooking pollock.\\n\\nThe common steps are:\\n- Preheat oven to 350°F (175°C).\\n- Season pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n- Bake for about 15 minutes until the fish is cooked and flakes easily.\\n\\nOptional step (from passage 3):\\n- Add cheese and let it melt for an additional 3 minutes after cooking.\\n\\nStep 3: Finalize the answer based on the synthesis.\\n\\nAnswer: To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place them on a baking sheet (optional: spray with butter flavored cooking spray), and bake for about 15 minutes until the fish is cooked and flakes easily. Optionally, top with cheese and return to the oven for 3 minutes to melt the cheese.\", \"Step 1: Preheat the oven. According to passage 2, preheat the oven to 350 degrees 