 the fold is on the bias.  \\n\\nAnswer: Fold each of the four corners of the quilt—lower right, lower left, top left, and top right—toward the center of the quilt, making sure each fold is made on the bias.\", \"Step 1: Lay the quilt on a flat surface such as a bed or table.\\nStep 2: Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\\nStep 3: Fold the lower left corner up toward the center of the quilt, again making sure the fold is on the bias.\\nStep 4: Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt, maintaining the bias fold.\\nStep 5: Finally, fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt, making sure this fold is also on the bias.\\n\\nAnswer: To fold a quilt, first lay it flat. Then fold each corner—lower right, lower left, top left, and top right—toward the center of the quilt, ensuring each fold is made on the bias.\", \"Step 1: Lay the quilt on a flat surface, such as a bed or table.\\nStep 2: Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\\nStep 3: Fold the lower left corner up toward the center of the quilt, again making sure the fold is on the bias.\\nStep 4: Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt with the fold on the bias.\\nStep 5: Fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that all corners are folded toward the center with the fold on the bias, which is suitable for preparing the quilt for mitered binding.\\n\\nAnswer: To fold a quilt, fold the lower right corner up toward the center, then the lower left corner up, followed by the top left corner down, and finally the top right corner down, ensuring each fold is on the bias.\", \"Step 1: Lay the quilt on a flat surface such as a bed or table.\\nStep 2: Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\\nStep 3: Fold the lower left corner up toward the center of the quilt, again making sure the fold is on the bias.\\nStep 4: Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt, maintaining the bias fold.\\nStep 5: Fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\\n\\nAnswer: To fold a quilt, fold each corner (lower right, lower left, top left, and top right) toward the center, ensuring each fold is made on the bias.\"]", "time_sec": 121.23, "generation_time_seconds": 121.2265, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.5, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
