is 0 inches annually.\\n   - The US average is 26 inches.\\n\\n4. **Sunshine**:\\n   - Sausalito has an average of 256 sunny days per year.\\n\\n5. **Comfort Index**:\\n   - Sausalito has a comfort index of 84 out of 100.\\n   - The US average is 54.\\n   - The comfort index is based on days within 70–80°F and penalized for excessive humidity.\\n\\n6. **Air Quality and Pollution**:\\n   - Air quality index is 13% better than the national average.\\n   - Pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\\n\\nOverall, Sausalito has a mild climate with moderate rainfall, no snow, and a high number of sunny days. The temperature is generally comfortable, as indicated by the comfort index, despite some contradictions in the data (e.g., \\\"most monthly precipitation in January with 0 inches\\\").\\n\\nAnswer: Sausalito has a mild climate with average temperatures ranging from a low of 43°F in January to a high of 69°F in July. It receives 34 inches of rain annually, with 56 days of measurable precipitation, and no snow. The city enjoys 256 sunny days per year and has a comfort index of 84 out of 100, indicating a generally comfortable climate.\", \"To determine the average weather in Sausalito, we can analyze the information provided in the passages.\\n\\n1. Temperature:\\n   - The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58°F in September.\\n   - The lowest monthly average temperature is 50°F in December.\\n   - The July high is around 69°F.\\n   - The January low is 43°F.\\n   These values indicate that Sausalito has mild temperatures throughout the year, with no extreme heat or cold.\\n\\n2. Precipitation:\\n   - The most monthly precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches (this appears to be an error, as it contradicts the statement that Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain annually).\\n   - However, passage 2 states that Sausalito receives 34 inches of rain per year.\\n   - The number of days with any measurable precipitation is 56.\\n   This suggests