 help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and remove splinters in the wilderness. These uses highlight their versatility and value in emergency situations.\\n\\nAnswer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize an arm by creating a makeshift sling, secure bandages over wounds, help close severe wounds when stitches aren't available, and remove splinters.\", \"Safety pins in a first aid box are used for multiple purposes in emergency situations. They can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to create a makeshift arm sling. They can also be used to secure a bandana over a wounded arm or leg to apply pressure and control bleeding. In dire circumstances, safety pins can help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches. Additionally, they can be used to remove splinters in the wilderness. These versatile uses make safety pins a valuable addition to a first aid kit.\\n\\nAnswer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used to create a makeshift arm sling, secure bandages over wounds, temporarily close severe wounds when stitches aren't available, and remove splinters.\", \"Step 1: Identify the main topic of the passage — the uses of safety pins in survival and first aid situations.\\n\\nStep 2: Extract relevant information from passage 2 about first aid uses of safety pins:\\n- Immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to the chest to create a makeshift arm sling.\\n- Secure a bandana over a wounded arm or leg.\\n- Help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\\n- Remove splinters in the wilderness.\\n\\nStep 3: Note the context — safety pins are mentioned as useful items in survival kits and first aid.\\n\\nStep 4: Synthesize the answer — safety pins in a first aid box can be used for immobilizing limbs, securing bandages, closing wounds, and removing splinters.\\n\\nFinal Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box can be used to immobilize an arm with a makeshift sling, secure bandages over wounds, close severe wounds when stitches aren't available, and remove splinters.\", \"Safety pins in a first aid box are used for multiple purposes in first aid situations. According to the passage, they can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to the chest to create a makeshift arm sling. They can also be used to secure a bandana over a wounded arm or leg to help control bleeding. In dire circumstances, safety pins can help keep a severe wound closed as a substitute for stitches. Additionally, safety pins can be used to remove splinters in the wilderness. These various uses demonstrate their versatility and value in a survival or first aid kit. \\n\\nAnswer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize limbs (e.g., creating a makeshift arm sling), secure bandages or bandanas over wounds, temporarily close severe wounds in place of stitches, and remove splinters.\"]", "time_sec": 118.885, "generation_time_seconds": 118.8813, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.26, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "539", "question": "lyrics he was a friend of mine", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are mentioned in the following passages:\n\n* Passage 1: In the context of the Greenbriar Boys recording the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" with singer Dian James in 1963.\n* Passage 2: As part of a fragmented repetition of the line \"He was a friend of mine\" in the passage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nPassage 1 and Passage 2", "pred": "\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun. And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\"", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the lyrics from the passage.\nFrom passage 2, the lyrics are:\n\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun.\"\n\nFrom passage 3, the lyrics are:\n\"And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\"\n\nStep 2: Combine the lyrics from both passages.\nThe complete lyrics consist of the lines from both passages, which are repeated throughout.\n\nStep 3: Present the full lyrics.\n\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun. And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\"\n\nAnswer: \"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun. And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\"", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the lyrics from the passage.\\nFrom passage 2, the lyrics are:\\n\\\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun.\\\"\\n\\nFrom passage 3, the lyrics are:\\n\\\"And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\n\\nStep 2: Combine the lyrics from both passages.\\nThe complete lyrics consist of the lines from both passages, which are repeated throughout.\\n\\nStep 3: Present the full lyrics.\\n\\\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun. And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\n\\nAnswer: \\\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun. And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\\\"\", \"Step 1: Identify the song title and context.\\nThe lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" are mentioned in the context of a song. The song has been recorded by multiple artists including Dian James and the Greenbriar Boys (1963), the Briarwood Singers (1963), Bobby Bare (1964), and Petula Clark (1964).\\n\\nStep 2: Determine the songwriters.\\nAccording to Passage 3, the songwriters of \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine\\\" are listed as Bob Dylan. This indicates that Bob Dylan is credited as the writer of the song.\\n\\nStep 3: Analyze the provided lyrics.\\nThe lyrics include:\\n- \\\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\n- \\\"He died without a penny he didn't have a dime.\\\"\\n- \\\"He died neath the midnight sun.\\\"\\n- \\\"And I never been quite satisfied.\\\"\\n- \\\"And he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\n- \\\"He never done no wrong.\\\"\\n- \\\"He never harmed no one.\\\"\\n- \\\"Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\n\\nThese lines match the sentiment and structure of a folk song about mourning a deceased friend, consistent with the historical context and recordings.\\n\\nStep 4: Integrate all information.\\nFrom the passages, we learn that multiple artists released versions of \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine\\\" in the 1960s. The song's lyrics are repeated in Passage 2 and further elaborated in Passage 3. The song's writer is Bob Dylan, and its theme centers on the loss of a friend.\\n\\nFinal answer:\\nThe lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" are from a folk song written by Bob Dylan. The song speaks of mourning the death of a friend, emphasizing his worthiness and the sorrow felt at his passing. It includes lines such as \\\"He died without a penny he didn't have a dime\\\" and \\\"Every time I hear his name, Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'.\\\" The song was recorded by various artists in the 1960s, including the Greenbriar Boys, Bobby Bare, and Petula Clark.\\n\\nAnswer: The lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" are from a folk song written by Bob Dylan, which expresses sorrow over the death of a friend and has been performed by multiple artists including the Greenbriar Boys\", \"Step-by-step reasoning:\\n\\n1. The query is asking for the lyrics to the song \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine.\\\"\\n2. Passage 2 contains the lyrics of the song in a direct form:  \\n   - \\\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun.\\\"\\n3. Passage 3 continues with additional lyrics:  \\n   - \\\"And I never been quite satisfied.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"And he was a friend of mine.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"He never done no wrong.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"He never done no wrong.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"A thousand miles from home.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"And he never harmed no one.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"And he was a friend of mine.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"He was a friend of mine.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"He was a friend of mine.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"Every time I hear his name.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'.\\\"  \\n   - \\\"Cause he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\n4. Combining the relevant parts from both passages, we get the full set of lyrics as provided.\\n5. The song is credited to Bob Dylan as the songwriter in passage 3.\\n\\nTherefore, the lyrics to \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine\\\" are derived from passages 2 and 3.\\n\\nAnswer: He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun. And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\", \"Step 1: Analyze the query and determine the focus of the question.\\nThe question is asking for the lyrics of the song \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine.\\\"\\n\\nStep 2: Review the provided passages for information about the song's lyrics.\\nPassage 2 contains a section of the lyrics:\\n\\\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun.\\\"\\n\\nPassage 3 also contains lyrics:\\n\\\"And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\n\\nStep 3: Combine the information from both passages to provide a comprehensive answer.\\nThe lyrics include multiple v